# ── Line endings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Force LF everywhere regardless of core.autocrlf on the machine. Without this a
# .sh checked out on Windows gets CRLF and dies on Linux: "bad interpreter: ^M".
# After adding this file to an existing repo, run once: git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only shells genuinely need CRLF. PowerShell is cross-platform now, so
# it stays on LF — uncomment only for scripts that must run on Windows alone.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# *.ps1 text eol=crlf

# ── Binary — never normalize, never diff, never text-merge ────────────────────
# `binary` is shorthand for `-text -diff -merge`.
# Mirrors the BINARY formats from universal.gitignore, so behaviour stays correct
# when a project deliberately re-includes one of them. Text-based datasets are
# deliberately absent: *.csv and *.tsv stay text and keep a readable diff.

